---
layout: default
---

{%- comment -%}
  Local override of al_folio_core's cv.liquid. Body is identical to the gem's;
  the only addition is the scoped <style> block below.

  Two defects it corrects, both from Bootstrap-era class names that have no rule
  in v1's Tailwind build (al_folio.compat.bootstrap.enabled is false here):

  1. Each CV entry is <li class="list-group-item"> inside
     <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">. `.list-group-flush` is undefined,
     so every entry rendered a stray disc bullet and a 40px indent.
  2. `.date-column` carries `text-center`, so date badges of differing widths
     ("2020 - Present" vs "2025 - 2025") started at different x positions and
     the column looked ragged.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  .cv .list-group {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .cv .list-group-item {
    list-style: none;
  }
  .cv .list-group-item::marker {
    content: "";
  }
  /* left-align the date/location column so badges form a clean edge */
  .cv .date-column {
    text-align: left;
  }
  .cv .date-column .table-cv {
    width: 100%;
  }
  .cv .date-column .badge {
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .cv .date-column .location {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* Highlights list: tighten the browser-default 40px indent, and match the
     1.5rem margin the entry title carries via `ml-md-4` so the bullets sit
     under the title instead of hanging out to its left. */
  .cv ul.items {
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .cv ul.items li {
    margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }
</style>

{% assign cv_feature_enabled = site.al_folio.features.cv.enabled | default: true %}

{% if site.plugins contains 'al_folio_cv' and cv_feature_enabled %}
  {% al_folio_cv_render %}
{% else %}
  <div class="post">
    <header class="post-header">
      <h1 class="post-title">{{ page.title }}</h1>
      <p class="post-description">CV rendering is unavailable.</p>
    </header>
    <article>
      <p>Enable the <code>al_folio_cv</code> plugin and set <code>al_folio.features.cv.enabled: true</code> to render this page.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
{% endif %}
